WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.988
The rest of the gaps are
about trust and reach.

2
00:00:02.988 --> 00:00:06.983
The sample prints raw identifiers
with no names and no tier,

3
00:00:06.983 --> 00:00:09.675
and a reviewer can't act on an identifier.

4
00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:13.650
It signs in without naming a
cloud or limiting its permissions.

5
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.460
Its transitive read uses beta
on a hard-coded worldwide host,

6
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.050
which is wrong for the government clouds.

7
00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:21.932
And it says nothing about Azure,

8
00:00:21.932 --> 00:00:25.912
where Owner and User Access
Administrator are just as privileged.

9
00:00:25.912 --> 00:00:30.106
So the verdict is: keep Learn's page
as the model and the cross-check,

10
00:00:30.106 --> 00:00:32.570
but don't use its loop as the inventory.
